{
  "uid": "n8n-system-tasks",
  "title": "n8n System Tasks",
  "tags": [
    "n8n",
    "system-tasks"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "auto",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "links": [
    {
      "title": "n8n Durable Scheduler",
      "type": "dashboards",
      "tags": [
        "scheduler"
      ],
      "asDropdown": false,
      "icon": "external link",
      "includeVars": false,
      "keepTime": true,
      "targetBlank": false,
      "tooltip": "The scheduler that runs durable system tasks",
      "url": ""
    }
  ],
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "task",
        "label": "System task",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(n8n_system_task_info, task)",
          "refId": "StandardVariableQuery"
        },
        "multi": true,
        "includeAll": true,
        "allValue": ".*",
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1
      },
      {
        "name": "instance",
        "label": "Main instance",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(n8n_system_task_info, instance)",
          "refId": "StandardVariableQuery"
        },
        "multi": true,
        "includeAll": true,
        "allValue": ".*",
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Tasks Not Scheduled",
      "description": "Tasks that n8n failed to schedule, so nothing will trigger them any more.\n\nWhen bad: above zero, that task will not run again until the main restarts or leadership moves. Find it on Overdue Factor, then read the main's logs for the scheduling error.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "min": 0
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "background"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "count(min by (task, mode) (n8n_system_task_scheduled{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"}) == 0) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "Tasks not scheduled"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Most Overdue Task",
      "description": "The task whose last success is furthest behind, counted in that task's own cadences. 1 means one cadence has passed, which is normal. 2 means it missed a full occurrence.\n\nWhen bad: above 2 the task missed at least one run. Above 3 and still rising, it has stopped. Check Tasks Not Scheduled, then Runs per Task for failures and Skipped Occurrences for overlap.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 4,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "decimals": 1,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 1.5
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          "min": 0
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "background"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "topk(1, (time() - max by (task) (n8n_system_task_last_success_timestamp_seconds{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"})) / max by (task) (n8n_system_task_interval_seconds{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"}))",
          "legendFormat": "{{task}}",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Runs Finished",
      "description": "How many system task runs finished in the selected range, successes and failures together. Runs that stopped cleanly at shutdown or leader handover are left out.\n\nWhen bad: if the total barely grows as you widen the range, the tasks are not running. Check Tasks Not Scheduled first, then Overdue Factor.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 10,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 5,
        "h": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "min": 0
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(increase(n8n_system_task_run_duration_seconds_count{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\", result=~\"success|failure\"}[$__range])) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "Runs finished"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Run Failure Rate",
      "description": "Share of finished runs that failed over the selected range. Runs that stopped cleanly at shutdown or leader handover are ignored.\n\nWhen bad: above about 1%, a task is erroring. Break it down on Runs per Task. One task points at that task's own dependency; every task points at the database or the host.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 15,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 5,
        "h": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 0.01
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.1
              }
            ]
          },
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "background"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(increase(n8n_system_task_run_duration_seconds_count{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\", result=\"failure\"}[$__range])) or vector(0)) / clamp_min(sum(increase(n8n_system_task_run_duration_seconds_count{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\", result=~\"success|failure\"}[$__range])), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Run Failure Rate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Runs In Flight",
      "description": "System task runs happening right now, across every task.\n\nWhen bad: a value that stays above zero for longer than that task's Run Duration p95 is a hung run. Its next occurrences appear on Skipped Occurrences as `overlap`.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 20,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "min": 0
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(n8n_system_task_runs_in_flight{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"}) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "Runs in flight"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Overdue Factor \u2014 Age of Last Success \u00f7 Cadence",
      "description": "How far each task's last success has fallen behind, counted in that task's own cadences. 1 is normal, 2 means a full occurrence was missed. The same thresholds work for a task that runs every 30 seconds and one that runs daily.\n\nA purple line at 1 on the right axis means the task is registered but has no recorded success. Expect this for a few minutes after a failover.\n\nWhen bad: a line above 2 missed an occurrence; above 3 and rising, the task has stopped. A purple line that lasts longer than one cadence means the task has never completed since the current leader took over.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "min": 0,
          "decimals": 2,
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "showPoints": "auto",
            "axisLabel": "cadences",
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "dashed"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "transparent",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 2
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 3
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": "/no success recorded$/"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "purple"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.axisPlacement",
                "value": "right"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.axisLabel",
                "value": "absent (1 = yes)"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.axisSoftMax",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.drawStyle",
                "value": "line"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.fillOpacity",
                "value": 15
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.thresholdsStyle",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "off"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [
                    8,
                    6
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ],
          "sortBy": "Last *",
          "sortDesc": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(time() - max by (task) (n8n_system_task_last_success_timestamp_seconds{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"})) / max by (task) (n8n_system_task_interval_seconds{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{task}}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "max by (task) (n8n_system_task_info{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"} unless on (task) n8n_system_task_last_success_timestamp_seconds{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{task}} \u2014 no success recorded"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Time to Next Run \u2014 In-Memory Timers",
      "description": "Seconds until the occurrence each in-memory timer is armed for. A timer re-arms itself the moment it fires, so a healthy task draws a sawtooth whose peaks are its own cadence, whatever its runs cost. Durable tasks have no armed timer and never appear here.\n\nWhen bad: a line that crosses zero and keeps falling is armed for a moment in the past, so it will never fire: the timer stopped planning. Check Tasks Not Scheduled, then the leader's logs. A brief dip below zero is only fire lag.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "showPoints": "auto",
            "axisSoftMin": 0,
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "dashed"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "transparent",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "min"
          ],
          "sortBy": "Last *",
          "sortDesc": false
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "asc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max by (task) (n8n_system_task_next_run_timestamp_seconds{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"}) - time()",
          "legendFormat": "{{task}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Runs per Task & Outcome",
      "description": "Finished runs per second, split by task and outcome. The height of the stack is total throughput. A run that stops cleanly at shutdown or leader handover shows as `aborted` and is not a failure.\n\nWhen bad: red on one task points at that task's own dependency; red on all of them points at the database or the host. A task whose stack disappears has stopped running: check Tasks Not Scheduled.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 20,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "showPoints": "auto",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": "/failure$/"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": "/aborted$/"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "blue"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "sortBy": "Max",
          "sortDesc": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (task, result) (rate(n8n_system_task_run_duration_seconds_count{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{task}} \u00b7 {{result}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Run Duration \u2014 p50 / p95",
      "description": "How long each task's runs take.\n\nWhen bad: p95 close to the task's own cadence means the next occurrence will overlap and be skipped; confirm on Skipped Occurrences. A p95 pinned at 10 minutes, the highest value this panel can show, means runs are effectively hung.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 13,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "showPoints": "auto"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": "/p50$/"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [
                    8,
                    6
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "sortBy": "Max",
          "sortDesc": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le, task) (rate(n8n_system_task_run_duration_seconds_bucket{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{task}} p50"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, task) (rate(n8n_system_task_run_duration_seconds_bucket{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{task}} p95"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Skipped Occurrences",
      "description": "Occurrences that came due but did not run, and why. `overlap` means the previous run was still going. `provisioned_elsewhere` means the durable scheduler owns the task. `aborted` means the occurrence fired during a leader handover. `coalesced` means the process slept through several occurrences and they merged into one late run. Only `overlap` is a problem.\n\nWhen bad: steady `overlap` means runs take longer than their cadence; compare with Run Duration p95. Steady `coalesced` means the host suspends, or the event loop is blocked.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 22,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 20,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "showPoints": "auto",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": "/overlap$/"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "orange"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": "/provisioned_elsewhere$/"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "purple"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": "/aborted$/"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "blue"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": "/coalesced$/"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "super-light-blue"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "sortBy": "Max",
          "sortDesc": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (task, reason) (rate(n8n_system_task_runs_skipped_total{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{task}} \u00b7 {{reason}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Timer Fire Lag \u2014 p50 / p99",
      "description": "How late each task starts, measured from the moment its occurrence was due.\n\nWhen bad: p50 above a second means the event loop is blocked. A p99 in hours means the host was suspended or is overloaded, and lines up with `coalesced` on Skipped Occurrences.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 22,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "showPoints": "auto"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": "/p50$/"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [
                    8,
                    6
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "sortBy": "Max",
          "sortDesc": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le, task) (rate(n8n_system_task_fire_lag_seconds_bucket{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{task}} p50"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le, task) (rate(n8n_system_task_fire_lag_seconds_bucket{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{task}} p99"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Retries & Provision-Check Failures",
      "description": "Retries are extra attempts after a failed run. A provision-check failure means n8n could not tell whether the durable scheduler owns the task, so it ran the task itself. That is the safe fallback, but it means a durable task could run twice.\n\nWhen bad: retries rising together with red on Runs per Task means a task keeps failing. Any provision-check failure points at the scheduler tables or the database connection: check the Durable Scheduler row.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "showPoints": "auto"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": "/provision-check failures$/"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "orange"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "sortBy": "Max",
          "sortDesc": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (task) (rate(n8n_system_task_retries_total{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{task}} retries"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum by (task) (rate(n8n_system_task_provision_check_failures_total{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{task}} provision-check failures"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Mode Split \u2014 In-Memory vs Durable",
      "description": "Runs per second by the path each run took: a timer on the leader main, or the durable scheduler. Every system task runs on a timer today, so `durable` stays flat at zero until system tasks are made durable.\n\nWhen bad: if both modes carry the same task at once, two paths are running it. Look for `provisioned_elsewhere` on Skipped Occurrences, which is how the timer is meant to stand down.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 31,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 20,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "showPoints": "auto",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "in_memory"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "blue"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "durable"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "green"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (mode) (rate(n8n_system_task_run_duration_seconds_count{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{mode}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": true,
      "title": "Leadership & Durable Scheduler (who runs each task?)",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 40,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": [
        {
          "id": 21,
          "type": "timeseries",
          "title": "Leaders per Task",
          "description": "How many mains are running each task. Exactly one main leads, so every line should sit at 1.\n\nWhen bad: 2 means two mains believe they lead, so the task runs twice; check leader election and clock skew. 0 means no main is running it, which is a gap in coverage rather than a quiet period.",
          "gridPos": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 41,
            "w": 8,
            "h": 9
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "short",
              "decimals": 0,
              "min": 0,
              "custom": {
                "lineWidth": 2,
                "fillOpacity": 0,
                "spanNulls": false,
                "showPoints": "auto",
                "thresholdsStyle": {
                  "mode": "dashed"
                }
              },
              "thresholds": {
                "mode": "absolute",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "color": "transparent",
                    "value": null
                  },
                  {
                    "color": "red",
                    "value": 2
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            "overrides": []
          },
          "options": {
            "legend": {
              "displayMode": "table",
              "placement": "bottom",
              "showLegend": true,
              "calcs": [
                "lastNotNull",
                "max"
              ],
              "sortBy": "Last *",
              "sortDesc": true
            },
            "tooltip": {
              "mode": "multi",
              "sort": "desc"
            }
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "refId": "A",
              "expr": "count by (task) (n8n_system_task_info{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\", mode=\"in_memory\"}) or (count by (task) (max_over_time(n8n_system_task_info{task=~\"$task\", instance=~\"$instance\", mode=\"in_memory\"}[$__range])) * 0)",
              "legendFormat": "{{task}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "type": "timeseries",
          "title": "Durable Scheduler \u2014 System Task Outcomes",
          "description": "The durable scheduler's own view of system task runs. Needs `N8N_METRICS_INCLUDE_SCHEDULER_METRICS=true`.\n\nEmpty is the expected reading today, because no system task is durable yet.\n\nWhen bad: failures here while Runs per Task stays green mean the task fails before its handler runs. Open the Durable Scheduler dashboard.",
